                                                                            <comments>
                            <comment id="493835" author="vitaly_fertman" created="Thu, 30 Apr 2026 00:00:46 +0000"  >&lt;p&gt;cancels are important, so we should not limit the amount of locks to be cancelled. at the same time limiting lh/rpc will result in longer RPC incoming queues. note that each RPC will require some mem allocated. therefore I do not think that having 100K RPCs x 100 locks each will have significant benefits vs 10k RPCs x 1k locks each - all of them must be handled asap. therefore I think we need to concentrate on how we can make cancel handling faster. &lt;/p&gt;

&lt;p&gt;first, is that hpreq_check just checks for HP without even cancelling locks, and later we will find them all again. and what we can do is to check only for the 1st lock there. e.g. ELC is never HP, because we can guarantee that all BL_AST locks are either get einval for BL_AST reply or CANCELs are sent separately. and we can do similar thing for CANCEL RPC as well - having only the 1st lock in CANCELs to be checked for HP.&lt;/p&gt;</comment>
